On Wed, Mar 18, 2015 at 11:17:47AM +0300, Solar Designer wrote:
> It was suggested to me off-list that it'd be helpful to publicly specify
> not only the date, but also the time (and timezone) of the forthcoming
> OpenSSL releases.  Can you?

Matt Caswell of OpenSSL has now clarified this on the openssl-* lists as
follows:

"I have received a number of queries regarding the timing of Thursday's
release. To clarify, we are aiming to have the release available
sometime between 1100-1500 GMT."

Alexander
